# Git workstream workflow (permanent)

## Core
- Branches = meaningful WORKSTREAMS / EPICS only. Not one branch per tiny tweak.
- Small related fixes = more commits on the active workstream branch.
- Default: REUSE the existing active workstream branch and its open PR.

## Canonical vs worktrees
- Permanent repo: `D:\Projects\SynTrack`
- Temp worktrees (not separate repos): `D:\Projects\SynTrack-client`, `D:\Projects\SynTrack-web`
- Never manually copy/move source between worktrees. Integrate via Git (PR → master).
- One worktree owns one branch; no cross-edit of another worktree’s branch/files/processes.

## Master
- Stable integration only. No direct development on master.
- Merge only after: implementation complete, tests green, live/visual acceptance, user acceptance, no blocking correctness issues.
- After merge: verify master has commits; delete remote+local feature branch; remove unused worktree; prune.
- Never hard-reset master blindly. Keep `archive/master-before-cleanup-2026-08-27` untouched.

## Current workstreams (examples)
- Desktop client → `feature/client` (PR #17 while open). Design, auth, BattleTag, roster, device linking, sync UI, settings, acceptance bugs, client tests/docs all stay here.
- Web → `feature/webapp` similarly.
- Do NOT create `feature/client-*`, `fix/client-*`, etc. while that milestone is open.

## New branch only when independent lifecycle
Parallel unrelated domain, risky experiment, urgent hotfix vs master, separate PR schedule, new epic after previous merged, or major conflict risk. “One small feature” is NOT enough.

## PRs
- One PR per unfinished workstream. Push updates to the same PR.
- Do not open follow-up PRs for small fixes on the same epic.

## Ops
- `npm run dev:stop` before switching branches in a worktree. Do not kill unrelated processes.
- Never touch `scripts/dev-manager.services.mjs`.
- Addon sync only if this workstream changed addons.
- Pre-commit: `npm verify` / git checks / `dotnet` as applicable.
- Rebase onto master before merge when needed; force-with-lease only after rebase (never `--force`).

## Status reporting (when starting phases)
Include: Workstream / Branch / Worktree / Existing PR / New branch created: YES/NO  
During an active epic, expect New branch created: NO.

## Before creating a branch/PR
Ask: existing active workstream? belongs there? needs independent lifecycle?  
If YES / YES / NO → reuse branch. If open PR exists → commit/push/update it.
